## 2. Core Architecture & System Boundaries

The Phase 3 architecture strictly enforces the **Deterministic-First Principle**. The AI Agent acts as an orchestrator and explainer; it does NOT calculate shortest paths or solve constraint batching directly.

```mermaid
graph TD
    FE["React Frontend (UI)"] -->|HTTP /api/v1/warehouse/*| API["FastAPI API Routers"]
    API -->|Delegates Request| SVC["WarehouseOptimizationService"]
    
    subgraph "Core Optimization Layer (Deterministic)"
        SVC -->|1. Load Layout| GRAPH["Warehouse Graph Engine (NetworkX / Custom)"]
        SVC -->|2. Form Batches| BATCH["Order Batching Engine (Heuristics / OR-Tools)"]
        SVC -->|3. Route Sequence| ROUTE["Pick Route Engine (A* / TSP Solver)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "AI Agent Orchestration & Explanation Layer"
        SVC -->|Optional AI Request| AGENT["Warehouse Agent"]
        AGENT -->|Invoke Approved Tools| TOOLS["Typed Agent Tool Interface (9 Tools)"]
        TOOLS -->|Call Internal API| SVC
        AGENT -->|Return Explanation & Diagnostics| SVC
    end
    
    SVC -->|Persist Results| DB[(PostgreSQL Database)]
```

### Architectural Guardrails:
* **No Direct Agent DB Access**: The agent cannot issue SQLAlchemy queries or SQL DML/DDL. All data reads occur via domain repositories; writes occur via service validation routines.
* **Deterministic Fallback**: If an LLM or agent provider is offline or times out, the core optimization engines execute deterministically and template-based explanations are returned.

