## 6. Pick Route Optimization Engine

### 6.1 Problem Formulation (Indoor Traveling Salesperson Problem)
Given a batch $B$ containing item set $I$, map each item to its storage location node $V_B \subseteq V$. The Pick Route Engine calculates a sequence $(v_0, v_1, v_2, \dots, v_k, v_0)$ where $v_0$ is the warehouse entrance/dispatch node, visiting all $v_i \in V_B$ with minimal total walking distance.

### 6.2 Routing Heuristics & Baseline Comparison

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Batch Picking Locations] --> B1[Input Order Baseline]
    A --> B2[Nearest Neighbor Heuristic]
    A --> B3[2-Opt / TSP Solver over Graph Matrix]
    
    B1 --> C1[High Distance, Backtracking]
    B2 --> C2[Medium Distance, Fast O-N^2]
    B3 --> C3[Optimal Short Distance, Low Backtracking]
```

1. **Input Order Baseline**: Visit locations in the order items appear in the order payload.
2. **Nearest Neighbor Heuristic**: Starting at entrance $v_0$, greedily visit the nearest unvisited pick location $v_{next}$ based on shortest graph distance $d(v_{current}, v_{next})$.
3. **Graph-Based 2-Opt TSP Optimizer (Recommended)**: Precompute pairwise shortest-path matrix between all target nodes using A*/Dijkstra, then apply 2-Opt edge swapping to eliminate path crossings.

