## 9. Performance Benchmark Methodology

To evaluate optimization efficiency quantitatively, benchmark scenarios are defined across three scaling dimensions.

### 9.1 Benchmark Test Matrix

```mermaid
gantt
    title Benchmark Execution Scale Matrix
    dateFormat  X
    axisFormat %s
    section Graph Pathfinding
    10 Nodes (Small Store)       :active, 0, 10
    100 Nodes (Medium Store)     :active, 0, 100
    1000 Nodes (Regional Hub)    :active, 0, 1000
    section Order Batching
    10 Pending Orders            :crit, 0, 10
    50 Pending Orders            :crit, 0, 50
    100 Pending Orders           :crit, 0, 100
    section Pick Routing
    5 Locations / Batch          :done, 0, 5
    20 Locations / Batch         :done, 0, 20
    50 Locations / Batch         :done, 0, 50
```

### 9.2 Measured Metrics:
1. **Algorithmic Execution Time ($ms$)**: Time required to solve graph paths, batches, and pick routes.
2. **Total Pick Distance ($m$)**: Cumulative meters walked to fulfill order batch.
3. **Batch Count Efficiency**: Number of batches generated vs optimal theoretical minimum.
4. **Distance Reduction Percentage ($\%$)**:

$$\text{Improvement } (\%) = \frac{\text{Distance}_{\text{Baseline}} - \text{Distance}_{\text{Optimized}}}{\text{Distance}_{\text{Baseline}}} \times 100$$

